<title>GERMANY: German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</title>
<headline>German government lowers yield on 5-yr Bobls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government is lowering the yield on its five-year Bundesobligationen bonds by raising the issue price of the paper to 99.70 from 99.55, the Bundesbank said on Friday.</p>
<p>The move, effective on Friday, brings the yield on the Series 122 4-1/2 percent paper to 4.56 percent from 4.60 percent.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 7565 1246</p>
